---
import LegalPage from "../../../components/app/LegalPage.astro";
import { localizedAlternates } from "../../../core/seo";

const title = "Privacy Policy – GiggleFace";
const canonicalPath = "/apps/giggleface/privacy-policy/";
const alternateLocales = localizedAlternates(
    canonicalPath,
    "/pt-br/apps/giggleface/privacy-policy/",
);
---

<LegalPage
    title={title}
    description="Privacy policy for GiggleFace."
    lang="en"
    favicon="/apps/giggleface/favicon.png"
    canonicalPath={canonicalPath}
    alternateLocales={alternateLocales}
>
    <h1>{title}</h1>

    <h4>Last updated: August 4, 2026</h4>

    <p>
        GiggleFace respects your privacy and is designed to keep camera, mask,
        facial landmark, audio, and video processing on your device. This policy
        explains the limited information used to operate and improve the app.
    </p>

    <h3>1. Accounts and Personal Information</h3>

    <p>
        GiggleFace does not require an account and does not ask you to provide your
        name, email address, phone number, contacts, or precise location to servers
        controlled by the developer.
    </p>

    <h3>2. Camera, Microphone, Photo Library, and Files</h3>

    <p>GiggleFace may request system permissions only when needed for app features:</p>

    <ul>
        <li><strong>Camera:</strong> to capture and process the front-camera image in real time.</li>
        <li><strong>Microphone:</strong> to include audio when you choose to record a video.</li>
        <li><strong>Photo Library:</strong> to import images you select and save recordings when requested.</li>
        <li><strong>Files and sharing:</strong> to import or export mask files through system interfaces you control.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        These permissions are managed by iOS or macOS and can be changed in system
        settings. Denying a permission may prevent the related feature from working.
    </p>

    <h3>3. On-Device Media and Face Processing</h3>

    <p>
        Camera frames, imported images, masks, audio, and recordings are processed
        locally on your device. GiggleFace does not upload this media to servers
        operated by the developer.
    </p>

    <p>
        GiggleFace uses temporary facial landmarks and contours to position masks.
        These landmarks are used only during processing, are not used to identify
        you, are not stored as a facial identity template, and are not sent to the
        developer or Himetrica.
    </p>

    <h3>4. Local Storage</h3>

    <p>
        Masks, editor settings, exported files, and recordings remain under your
        control on your device and in locations you choose, such as Apple Photos,
        Files, iCloud, or another service selected through the system Share Sheet.
        Retention and deletion of those files are controlled by you and the selected
        storage provider.
    </p>

    <h3>5. Anonymous Analytics and Error Diagnostics</h3>

    <p>
        GiggleFace uses Himetrica to understand feature usage and diagnose technical
        errors. The integration is configured without Himetrica's identify function
        and does not send your name, email address, camera image, imported images,
        masks, audio, video, recordings, or facial landmarks.
    </p>

    <p>The limited diagnostic information may include:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>Randomly generated visitor and session identifiers;</li>
        <li>App screens or features used and session timing;</li>
        <li>App, operating system, and device version information;</li>
        <li>Error messages, stack traces, and technical context that does not contain media content.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        When the device is offline, diagnostic events may be queued locally and sent
        when connectivity returns. Network information, including an IP address, may
        be processed by Himetrica and its infrastructure for delivery, security, and
        approximate geographic statistics as described in Himetrica's policy.
        Detailed analytics are retained according to the developer's Himetrica plan.
    </p>

    <p>
        Learn more in Himetrica's
        <a href="https://www.himetrica.com/docs/swift" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Swift SDK documentation</a>
        and
        <a href="https://www.himetrica.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>6. Purchases</h3>

    <p>
        GiggleFace Premium is offered as a one-time in-app purchase. Apple processes
        payment, purchase verification, restoration, and refunds under its own terms.
        The developer does not receive your complete payment card information.
    </p>

    <h3>7. Sharing and Virtual Camera Use</h3>

    <p>
        When you export a mask or recording, the system Share Sheet sends the selected
        file only to the app or service you choose. Those third parties process the
        file under their own privacy policies.
    </p>

    <p>
        When you select GiggleFace as a macOS virtual camera, the processed camera feed
        becomes available to the communication app you selected. Services such as
        Google Meet, Microsoft Teams, or FaceTime may transmit, display, or record that
        feed according to their settings and policies. GiggleFace does not control how
        those services handle a call.
    </p>

    <h3>8. Data Sharing and Advertising</h3>

    <p>
        We do not sell or rent personal information and do not use your data for
        targeted advertising. Information is disclosed only to Himetrica for the
        limited analytics described above, to Apple for purchases and platform
        services, or to a service you intentionally select for sharing, storage, or
        communication.
    </p>

    <h3>9. Data Retention and Your Choices</h3>

    <p>
        The developer does not maintain a remote media library or named user account
        for GiggleFace. You can remove local masks and recordings using the app,
        Photos, Files, or the applicable storage service. Anonymous diagnostic data is
        retained under Himetrica's applicable retention period and may not be directly
        linkable to a named person.
    </p>

    <h3>10. Security</h3>

    <p>
        We minimize the information sent outside your device and apply reasonable
        technical safeguards. No method of electronic storage or transmission is
        completely secure, and third-party services remain responsible for their own
        systems.
    </p>

    <h3>11. Children's Privacy</h3>

    <p>
        GiggleFace is not designed to knowingly collect personal information from
        children. If you believe information has been handled in conflict with this
        policy, please contact us so the issue can be reviewed.
    </p>

    <h3>12. Changes to This Policy</h3>

    <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy to reflect product, technical, or legal
        changes. The latest version and its effective date will remain available on
        this page.
    </p>

    <h3>13. Contact</h3>

    <p>
        For questions about this Privacy Policy or GiggleFace, contact:
        <a href="mailto:adrianosouzacostaios@gmail.com">adrianosouzacostaios@gmail.com</a>
    </p>
</LegalPage>
